---

## Format

```
- ✓ [short-slug](url) — what it establishes, and what it changes here. → [notes]({{PRIOR_WORK_DIR}}/<topic>.md)
```

**The marker is the point.** Citation integrity is the one thing a research
phase can get catastrophically wrong, because a plausible-looking reference that
does not exist is indistinguishable from a real one at a glance.

- `✓` — retrieved and read. The claim on this line is checked against the source.
- `~` — abstract or summary only. Do not quote a number from it.
- `✗` — **searched for and not found**, or found and refuted. Keep these. A
  recorded absence is what stops the same fruitless search next quarter, and it
  is the only honest way to say "the literature does not cover this."

**Write what it changes here, not what it is about.** "Establishes kNN over
hidden states works at 10^8 scale, so our retrieval step is assembly, not
novelty" earns its line. "A paper about retrieval" does not.

## When it grows

Do not delete. **Group**: once a topic has several sources, collapse them into
one `{{PRIOR_WORK_DIR}}/<topic>.md` and leave a single line here pointing at it.
The individual papers keep living inside that document. Grouping is what keeps
this index an index — an entry per paper read would become a bibliography nobody
loads{{IF PRIOR_WORK_CAP}}, and the cap is what forces the grouping to actually
happen{{ENDIF}}.

